KNOWN BUGS:
_____________________________________________________________________

* Some systems have trouble linking with GNU Guile.  In their specific
  cases, adding "-lguile" to LDLIBS macro will work.  I wonder how to
  make this more robust in the autoconf?

_____________________________________________________________________

THINGS TO DO:
_____________________________________________________________________

* Improve the graphics, to make everything look better.  I think I
  need a graphic designer to help me do this.  GTK+ would be nice.

* Move all the robot_* variables into a single struct.  Keep "robot"
  as a pointer to the current robot, so that robot_x becomes
  robot->x.  This will help in later versions when we have network
  support.

* In version 2.0, more creatures will get added.  The things called
  "baddie" and "food" and "prize" will be generic descriptors.  For
  example, "food" will be a generic name for "cookie" or "donut", so
  that (robot-feel 'cookie) will fail if the thing is a donut, but
  (robot-feel 'food) will still work.

* Add number of units walked, and number of shots to the statistics.
